  "summary": "I added a \"Tour\" button below the canvas, in `src/main.ts`. It typechecks, and the render shows the button below the canvas with the overview drawing normally. I did not run the tour itself, because the render tool can't click.\n\n- **Tour:** Clicking \"Tour\" focuses each planet in turn, from Mercury out to Neptune, for 3 seconds each. The info panel shows for each planet. At the end the camera returns to the overview and the button goes back to \"Tour\".\n- **Stop tour:** While touring the button reads \"Stop tour\". Clicking it ends the tour and returns to the overview.\n- **Other ways to end the tour:** Clicking a planet or empty space, pressing Escape, or calling `__focusPlanet`/`__unfocus` also ends the tour. Escape and `__unfocus` return to the overview. A planet click or `__focusPlanet` moves the camera to that planet instead.\n- **Timing:** Tour timing uses real time, so the tour keeps going while orbital motion is paused.\n- **State:** `window.__TASK_STATE__` now has a read-only `touring` boolean."
}